    "bottomLine": "The inlet to buy for a 30-amp setup, especially if you are installing an interlock rather than a Reliance kit.",
    "description": "A power inlet box is the part of a generator hookup that lives outside: a weatherproof box on the wall with a male inlet where the generator cord plugs in. The PB30 is Reliance's 30-amp version, with an L14-30 inlet that mates with the matching connector on a standard 30-amp, four-wire generator cord. Inside the house it is wired to either a manual transfer switch or, with an interlock kit, a dedicated generator breaker in the main panel. If you buy a Reliance CRK kit you already have one, so do not buy it twice. Where it earns its own place in this list is the interlock route: interlock kits supply the panel hardware, not the inlet, so you need an inlet box regardless. Mount it where the generator can sit outdoors well away from windows, doors and vents, and keep the cord run reasonably short. The male inlet cannot be energized unless the cord is connected to a running generator, which is exactly why the inlet is male and the cord end is female."
  },
  {
    "id": "reliance-pbn50",
    "name": "Reliance Controls PBN50 Power Inlet Box",
