          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Will a transfer switch work with an inverter generator?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the generator's outlets. Many inverter generators are 120-volt only, which cannot properly feed a standard 120/240-volt switch or run any 240-volt load. Larger inverter models with an L14-30 outlet work with a 30-amp switch like any other generator. For a small 120-volt inverter, a single-circuit furnace switch is often the better match. Ask your electrician before connecting anything."
          }
        }
